### FinSight v2 - Manual Verification Postman / HTTP Client Checklist
### Run these sequentially against the running Spring Boot application (localhost:8080)

### 1. Register Users
### Register ADMIN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin Tester",
  "email": "admin_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### Register ANALYST
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Analyst Tester",
  "email": "analyst_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### Register VIEWER
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Viewer Tester",
  "email": "viewer_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}

### 2. Login as ADMIN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}

> {% 
    client.global.set("admin_access_token", response.body.data.accessToken); 
    client.global.set("admin_refresh_token", response.body.data.refreshToken);
%}

### 3. Fail login 5 times in a row (Lockout test)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "viewer_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### (Run the above 5 times, then run with correct password - expect 423 Locked)

### 4. Call /api/auth/refresh
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{admin_refresh_token}}"
}

> {% 
    client.global.set("admin_access_token", response.body.data.accessToken); 
    // Now the old refresh token is invalid. Replaying it should 401.
%}

### 5. Create a record with idempotencyKey
POST http://localhost:8080/api/records
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "adminId": 1,
  "amount": 150.00,
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "category": "Office Supplies",
  "recordDate": "2026-08-18",
  "description": "Purchased pens",
  "idempotencyKey": "idem-key-001"
}

### (Run the above twice, confirm 200 OK and no duplicate on second run)

### 6. Update Record (Optimistic Locking)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/records/1
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "adminId": 1,
  "amount": 200.00,
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "category": "Office Supplies",
  "recordDate": "2026-08-18",
  "description": "Purchased pens and paper",
  "version": 0 
}

### (Run again with version 0, expect 409 Conflict)

### 7. As VIEWER, attempt POST /api/records
### First login as VIEWER
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "viewer_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}
> {% client.global.set("viewer_access_token", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### Try to create
POST http://localhost:8080/api/records
Authorization: Bearer {{viewer_access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "adminId": 3,
  "amount": 50.00,
  "type": "EXPENSE",
  "category": "Snacks",
  "recordDate": "2026-08-18"
}
### Expect 403 Forbidden

### 8. As ADMIN, check Audit Log
GET http://localhost:8080/api/admin/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}

### Expect 200 and list of CREATE_RECORD, UPDATE_RECORD etc.

### 9. As ANALYST, call export report
### First login as ANALYST
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "analyst_test@finsight.com",
  "password": "password"
}
> {% client.global.set("analyst_access_token", response.body.data.accessToken); %}

### Request Export
POST http://localhost:8080/api/reports/export?userId=2&period=2026-08
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst_access_token}}

### Poll Export Status (replace jobId)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/reports/export/1
Authorization: Bearer {{analyst_access_token}}
